MCP Terminal Docker Integration
*******************************

This manual describes the ‘mcp-terminal-docker’ Debian package (version
0.1.0), which installs host integration for the MCP Terminal HTTPS
service running in Docker.

* Menu:

* Overview::                    What the package installs
* Commands::                    mcp-terminal-docker and mcp-terminal-info
* Configuration::               Host paths and JSON config
* Service::                     systemd and container lifecycle
* Sandbox::                     Worker images and project paths
* Install::                     Installing on a clean host
* Uninstall::                  remove and purge behavior


File: mcp-terminal-docker.info,  Node: Overview,  Next: Commands,  Prev: Top,  Up: Top

1 Overview
**********

The package:

   • pulls the matching service image from Docker Hub on install or
     upgrade;
   • pulls sandbox worker images (‘python-dev’, ‘node-dev’,
     ‘base-tools’);
   • creates host user ‘mcp-terminal’ for log and data directory
     ownership;
   • starts container ‘mcp-terminal’ publishing host port 3011 by
     default;
   • mounts ‘/var/run/docker.sock’ so the service can spawn sandbox
     containers;
   • registers ‘man’ and ‘info’ documentation.

   Host log and data directories are owned by
‘mcp-terminal:mcp-terminal’.


