2 Commands
**********

 -- Command: mcp-terminal-docker COMMAND

‘start’
     Start ‘mcp-terminal-docker.service’.
‘stop’
     Stop the service and container.
‘restart’
     Restart the same container instance.
‘recreate’
     Remove and recreate the container (after config, certificate, or
     bind-mount changes).
‘status’
     Show systemd and container status.
‘info’
     Same summary as ‘mcp-terminal-info’.

 -- Command: mcp-terminal-info
     Print host integration summary (port, paths, image tag, container
     state).

   See also ‘man mcp-terminal-docker’, ‘man mcp-terminal-info’, and ‘man
mcp-terminal-config’ (JSON schema and field dependencies).


