6 Install
*********

On a clean Debian/Ubuntu host:

     sudo dpkg -i mcp-terminal-docker_0.1.0_amd64.deb
     sudo apt -f install
     mcp-terminal-info

   ‘apt -f install’ resolves package dependencies including ‘docker.io’.

   Place TLS material under ‘/etc/mcp-terminal/mtls_certificates/’
before first start if registration uses HTTPS.


File: mcp-terminal-docker.info,  Node: Uninstall,  Prev: Install,  Up: Top

7 Uninstall
***********

     sudo apt remove mcp-terminal-docker
     sudo apt purge mcp-terminal-docker

   On ‘apt purge’, maintainer scripts stop systemd, remove the
container, and remove the saved service Docker image using
‘/usr/lib/mcp-terminal/image-spec’ and/or a saved ref under
‘/var/lib/mcp-terminal/’.


